WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.070
I'm becoming nonfunctional
practically, and it doesn't bother me

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.065
as much that people think that
I'm weird, or crazy, or drunk.

00:00:11.065 --> 00:00:14.220
People think that I'm drunk,
really, I'm Tim Moutafis.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.910
I'm 62 years old.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.250
I'm an entrepreneur,
specializing in medical devices.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.780
I have two boys, who are grown.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:30.890
I have a wonderful wife, and I'm
looking to better my condition

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:31.925
to where it was before.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.610
When he got the diagnosis,
we were stunned.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.340
He's always been an
athlete, and not just, you

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.270
know, the weekend
warrior type, but we're

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.200
talking like biking
across Greece, and boxing,

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.040
and doing all these other things.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.380
And I think my initial reaction
was panic, like how can this be?

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.690
Every time I have a challenge,
I'm tempted to resolve it.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.390
So I saw this as an opportunity
to show who I am really.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:13.970
He was determined to act as if this were
a minor inconvenience, and that I think

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:20.890
was the thing that really got me
to stop panicking and to think,

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.651
OK, I got to approach
this in a different way.

00:01:23.651 --> 00:01:25.400
I mean I don't know
what I would have done

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.480
if he had just-- he you got
that diagnosis and said,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.050
oh my god, I'm done.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.125
These three traces are
of three electrodes.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.154
The top one is the anterior one.

00:02:51.154 --> 00:02:53.082
The middle one is in the middle.

00:02:53.082 --> 00:02:55.974
And this one is a posterior one.

00:02:55.974 --> 00:02:58.140
So, right now it's pretty quiet.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.035
Kind of like in a oscilloscope
this is a one second sweep.

00:03:01.035 --> 00:03:04.140
And when we see neurons, you'll see
the little vertical deflections.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.062
Those are single action
potentials of neurons, OK?

00:03:19.359 --> 00:03:21.359
Ok, so I'm going to stop
here for just a second,

00:03:21.359 --> 00:03:23.331
and check the impedence
of the electrodes,

00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:25.622
now that I'm confident that
they're out of the cannula.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:43.970
My first concern was what do I say to
my kids, because that was a concern.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.560
And, you know, kids are very good.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.360
They pick up on things.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.830
You don't have to say a whole lot.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.800
They kind of can see
where things are going.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.930
And so I did talk to them about it.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.280
But they also took their
cues from their dad,

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:05.010
who once he was diagnosed with
Parkinson's, within the first couple

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.652
of years said, OK, so
let me make up a plan

00:04:08.652 --> 00:04:10.610
here that I think will
help me in the long run.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:14.820
So windsurfing was something he
took up after he was diagnosed with

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:15.320
Parkinson's.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:30.660
Part of my protective nature is I want
to make it all better, like right away.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.640
And I've learned to trust him.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:39.535
Initially, when we started
windsurfing, which, you know,

00:04:39.535 --> 00:04:42.860
it was-- and on the open water.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.135
OK, we're talking ocean.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.400
It scared me to death.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.610
And I was all over him.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.610
Do you remember that one
time the coast guard came by?

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.370
I took a long rope, and I
tied myself to the shore.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.760
And then I windsurfed
the best way I could,

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.635
so it took me a couple
of seconds to do that.

00:05:01.635 --> 00:05:03.550
This is out on the open ocean.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.481
OK, so that scared me a little bit.

00:05:05.481 --> 00:05:06.856
Wait, you tied yourself to shore?

00:05:06.856 --> 00:05:07.356
Right.

00:05:07.356 --> 00:05:10.124
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:10.124 --> 00:05:11.290
Like, how long was the rope?

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.640
It was about a 1,000 feet or so.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.710
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.805
I mean, I was able to go back and
forth, but if there was a boat

00:05:17.805 --> 00:05:21.760
to cross the rope, then we
would have had a problem.

00:05:33.712 --> 00:05:35.704
OK, we're going to go
ahead and get started.

00:05:35.704 --> 00:05:37.198
Open and close your hand.

00:05:39.188 --> 00:05:39.688
Good.

00:05:39.688 --> 00:05:40.313
The light bulb.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.170
Show me how you turn a screw driver.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:46.660
Good.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.154
Say, I love tapioca pudding.

00:05:48.154 --> 00:05:49.648
I love tapioca pudding.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:50.644
OK, alright.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:03.710
Do it again.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.751
Open and close your hand.

00:06:06.512 --> 00:06:07.285
That looks good.

00:06:07.285 --> 00:06:08.160
Do the light bulb.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.245
Nice, how's it feel to you?

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:11.530
Same?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:12.030
Better?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:12.640
Or worse?

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.014
Same to better.

00:06:16.014 --> 00:06:17.165
Same to better.

00:06:17.165 --> 00:06:18.081
It looks looser to me.

00:06:18.081 --> 00:06:18.975
It looks more fluid.

00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:19.869
Try it again.

00:06:19.869 --> 00:06:20.940
Open both of your hands.

00:06:22.155 --> 00:06:22.975
Do the light bulb.

00:06:24.863 --> 00:06:26.327
Any unusual sensation Numbness?

00:06:26.327 --> 00:06:26.827
Tingling?

00:06:26.827 --> 00:06:27.809
Anything like that?

00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:32.228
You OK?

00:06:32.228 --> 00:06:33.210
No.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.183
No, you're not OK?

00:06:34.183 --> 00:06:34.683
No I'm not.

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:40.575
Is he having trouble talking?

00:06:41.739 --> 00:06:43.030
There is a little face pulling.

00:06:45.485 --> 00:06:46.958
Ok go back down.

00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:47.931
To four?

00:06:47.931 --> 00:06:48.431
To zero.

00:06:48.431 --> 00:06:49.934
OK, feel better now?

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:50.434
Yeah.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:57.200
And, you know, this is a
really like quick and dirty

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:02.510
test, so it's much finer when you
get it tested in the office, OK?

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.688
So, I'm just going to
secure everything in place.

00:07:07.688 --> 00:07:08.438
And then close up.

00:07:08.438 --> 00:07:10.854
Feel free to relax, close your
eyes, take a nap, whatever.

00:07:10.854 --> 00:07:11.402
That's fine.

00:07:11.402 --> 00:07:12.878
OK.

00:07:12.878 --> 00:07:13.378
You ok?

00:07:15.348 --> 00:07:15.848
Great job!

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.350
I think there's a lot of hope
in terms of what's out there.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.101
So, there's so much
research going on right now.

00:07:30.101 --> 00:07:36.070
So, I'm hopeful that the deep brain
stimulator will give us-- buy us

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:41.658
some time until the next big thing,
and then we'll go from there.

